{"id":"trahison","lemma":"trahison","pos":"noun","rank":2472,"glosses":["treason","betrayal","pitfall"],"ipa":"/tʁa.i.zɔ̃/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/be/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-VictorDtmtc-trahison.wav/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-VictorDtmtc-trahison.wav.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"plural":"trahisons"},"formAudio":{"trahisons":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/84/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Eihel-trahisons.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Il est capable de trahison.","en":"He is capable of treachery.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"is","l":"être"},{"g":"able, capable"},{"g":"of / from"},null]},{"text":"Cela pourrait être interprété comme un acte de trahison.","en":"This could be construed as an act of treason.","words":[{"g":"that"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"pouvoir"},{"g":"to be"},{"g":"to translate","l":"interpréter"},{"g":"as"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"act"},{"g":"of / from"},null]},{"text":"Quelques-uns l'accusèrent même de trahison.","en":"Some even accused him of treason.","words":[{"g":"some","l":"quelque"},{"g":"a, an","l":"un"},{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"to accuse","l":"accuser"},{"g":"same"},{"g":"of / from"},null]},{"text":"Il fut exilé sur une île pour haute trahison.","en":"He was banished to an island for high treason.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"bole","l":"fût"},{"g":"exiled, in exile"},{"g":"on"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"island"},{"g":"for"},{"g":"high society"},null]},{"text":"La complicité avec l'ennemi est considérée comme de la trahison.","en":"Aiding and abetting the enemy is considered treason.","words":[{"g":"the / her"},{"g":"complicity"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"enemy"},{"g":"is","l":"être"},null,{"g":"as"},null,null,null],"phrases":[[8,10,"of the"]]}]}